{"name":"Sponge Cake","hex":"#fffe40","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sponge cake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light, soft, baked dessert (commonly layered with cream and jam) that is typically made with flour, sugar, baking powder and eggs, and has a firm, yet well aerated structure, similar to that of a sea sponge.","Something that is simple or very easy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponge_cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sponge cake","blocks":[{"text":"Sponge cake is a light cake made with egg whites, flour and sugar, sometimes leavened with baking powder. Most sponge cakes contain egg yolks, but some do not, such as angel food cake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Victoria_Sponges.jpg/330px-Victoria_Sponges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sponge_cake"},{"title":"Sponge","blocks":[{"text":"Sponges or sea sponges are primarily marine invertebrates of the animal phylum Porifera. They are filter feeders that are typically bound to the seabed, being sessile. Sponges are one of the most ancient members of living seabed community (macrobenthos), with many species being important reef-builders. Some sponge species inhabit freshwater."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sponges_in_Caribbean_Sea%2C_Cayman_Islands.jpg/330px-Sponges_in_Caribbean_Sea%2C_Cayman_Islands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sponge"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/HK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_Goh_Jan-2013.JPG/500px-HK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_Goh_Jan-2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/HK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_Goh_Jan-2013.JPG/1280px-HK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_Goh_Jan-2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/HK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_Goh_Jan-2013.JPG/500px-HK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_Goh_Jan-2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Steamed sponge cake known as ma lai gao (Malay sponge cake)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHK_Sheung_Wan_%E5%AF%B6%E6%B9%96%E9%87%91%E5%AE%B4_Treasure_Lake_Seafood_Restaurant_food_Chinese_Steamed_Sponge_Cake_%E9%A6%AC%E6%8B%89%E7%B3%95_Mah_Lai_